# OpenSpec extra for {{ project_name }}

This tree is copied only when `openspec_extra=enabled`. It is **off by default**
on generated projects. The Riso maintainer repo uses OpenSpec; generated apps
opt in.

## Layout

```text
openspec/
├── AGENTS.md              # Agent workflow for this extra
├── config.yaml            # spec-driven schema + project context
├── USAGE.md               # this file
├── specs/                 # Source of truth (current behavior)
│   └── <domain>/spec.md
└── changes/               # Proposed work (one folder per change)
    ├── <change-name>/
    │   ├── proposal.md
    │   ├── design.md
    │   ├── tasks.md
    │   └── specs/<domain>/spec.md
    └── archive/           # Completed changes after archive
```

If `openspec/specs/` is empty after generate, add domain specs as
`openspec/specs/<domain>/spec.md` (one folder per capability).

## Workflow

1. Propose: create `openspec/changes/<change-name>/` with proposal, specs, design, tasks.
2. Apply: implement the task checklist.
3. Archive: merge delta specs into `openspec/specs/` and move the change under `archive/`.

Delta specs use `## ADDED Requirements`, `## MODIFIED Requirements`, and
`## REMOVED Requirements`. Requirements use RFC 2119 keywords (MUST / SHALL /
SHOULD / MAY) and testable scenarios.

## CLI (optional)

These files are the extra. Installing an OpenSpec CLI is optional and is **not**
added as a generated dependency. If you already have `openspec` on PATH:

```bash
openspec list
openspec validate
```

`mise.toml` always renders and is not gated by this extra.
